Package: NetSimR
Type: Package
Title: Actuarial Functions for Non-Life Insurance Modelling
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Yiannis", "Parizas", email = "yiannis.parizas@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-0523-0751"))
Description: Assists actuaries and other insurance modellers in pricing,
    reserving and capital modelling for non-life insurance and
    reinsurance modelling. Provides functions that help model
    excess levels, capping and pure Incurred but not reported
    claims (pure IBNR).
    Includes capped mean, exposure curves and increased limit
    factor curves (ILFs) for LogNormal, Gamma, Pareto, Sliced
    LogNormal-Pareto and Sliced Gamma-Pareto distributions.
    Includes mean, probability density function (pdf), cumulative
    probability function (cdf) and inverse cumulative probability
    function for Sliced LogNormal-Pareto and Sliced Gamma-Pareto
    distributions.
    Includes calculating pure IBNR exposure with LogNormal and
    Gamma distribution for reporting delay.
    Includes claims reserving: the chain ladder with Mack's standard
    errors and tail factors, Bornhuetter-Ferguson, Benktander and Cape
    Cod methods, a bootstrap of the reserves, the one-year view of
    Merz and Wuthrich, the Munich chain ladder of paid and incurred
    claims, the growth curves of Clark (2003), a chain ladder for claims
    inflation, and actual against expected development.
    Includes the discounting of reserves and a risk adjustment for
    'IFRS' 17, and the 'Solvency II' standard formula's non-life premium
    and reserve risk. Includes a Tweedie family for generalised linear
    models of the loss cost, rate reviews with on-level premiums and
    Buhlmann-Straub credibility, the simulation of portfolios of several
    lines joined by a Gaussian or t copula, with value at risk, tail value
    at risk and capital allocation, and the comparison of reinsurance
    programmes.
    Includes excess of loss reinsurance pricing: the burning cost, a
    Pareto model of the large losses, exposure rating with the MBBEFD
    exposure curves of Bernegger (1997) <doi:10.2143/AST.27.1.563208>
    or a claim size distribution, and the
    technical premium with reinstatements.
    Includes six 'shiny' tools: a claims simulator with reinsurance
    structures, a generalised linear model fitting tool with rate tables,
    a claims frequency and severity distribution fitting tool, a claims
    reserving tool, a reinsurance pricing tool and a portfolio capital
    tool.
    Methods used in the package refer to
    Free for All by Yiannis Parizas (2023) <https://www.theactuary.com/2023/03/02/free-all>;
    Escaping the triangle by Yiannis Parizas (2019) <https://www.theactuary.com/features/2019/06/2019/06/05/escaping-triangle>;
    Taken to excess by Yiannis Parizas (2019) <https://www.theactuary.com/features/2019/03/2019/03/06/taken-excess>.
